      "locked": false,
      "text": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\nThere is no pane header. The compact top bar is the screen's own: tabs and ＋ (New tab) on the left. Docked, the right side has Open in a separate window (⧉), More (⋯), Expand over the conversation (⤢) and Close the browser (✕).\nDetached, it has Dock beside the conversation, More and Close the window.\n⋯ menu: the tabs that do not fit (when there is more than one), then Reload F5 and Close this tab, then Switch the browser off… or Start the browser, then Open in a separate window or Dock beside the conversation.\nThe docked column defaults to 45% of the space beside the sessions sidebar. Drag the divider to resize it.\nThe detached window is titled \"<tab title> · <conversation title>\".\nA Read-only token sees \"Watching only: this token cannot act in the browser.\" under the address bar, and the controls are greyed out.\nSwitching it off asks \"Switch the browser off?\" (Switch off). While switched on but not running, it says \"The browser is switched on but not running\".\nRight-clicking a tab offers Show this tab and Close this tab. Ctrl+L goes to the address field (cue: \"Enter a web address\").\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
      "originalText": "Reference: briareus-windows. Other clients match this structure, differing only as noted here.\nThere is no pane header. The compact top bar is the screen's own: tabs and ＋ (New tab) on the left. Docked, the right side has Open in a separate window (⧉), More (⋯), Expand over the conversation (⤢) and Close the browser (✕).\nDetached, it has Dock beside the conversation, More and Close the window.\n⋯ menu: the tabs that do not fit (when there is more than one), then Reload F5 and Close this tab, then Switch the browser off… or Start the browser, then Open in a separate window or Dock beside the conversation.\nThe docked column defaults to 45% of the space beside the sessions sidebar. Drag the divider to resize it.\nThe detached window is titled \"<tab title> · <conversation title>\".\nA Read-only token sees \"Watching only: this token cannot act in the browser.\" under the address bar, and the controls are greyed out.\nSwitching it off asks \"Switch the browser off?\" (Switch off). While switched on but not running, it says \"The browser is switched on but not running\".\nRight-clicking a tab offers Show this tab and Close this tab. Ctrl+L goes to the address field (cue: \"Enter a web address\").\nRegion names (sidebar, canvas, raise, sunken) are the theme.* roles; widths and margins are layout.* in tokens/. Greys only, on purpose.",
